    "model_name": "Reliability-sensitive information-flow failure model",
    "core_question": "Why can multi-agent AI perform worse than the intended baseline?",
    "mechanism": "Multi-agent coordination can propagate, incorporate, or amplify unreliable information. When information from agents is treated as usable shared evidence, the system's collective reasoning state can become less reliable than the information available from reliable agents alone.",
    "mechanistic_chain": [
      "Agent-level information has heterogeneous reliability.",
      "Agents communicate information into a shared reasoning process.",
      "Unreliable information can enter that shared information state.",
      "Downstream reasoning can condition on contaminated shared information.",
      "The resulting collective state can produce an incorrect final answer.",
      "Therefore, adding agents does not guarantee improved performance."
    ],
